# Sebastian Software Skills

<!-- mdtheme:badges:start -->
<!-- mdtheme:badges:end -->

**Practical skills for AI agents, from product decisions to software delivery
and growth.**

Six independently installable skills help your agent make domain decisions,
avoid common mistakes, and verify its work. Each skill loads focused references
when the task needs them.

**[Explore the collection →](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/)**
Use cases, example prompts, strengths, and the full scope live on the homepage.

## What's Included

| Skill | Use it for |
| --- | --- |
| [`effective-product`](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/skills/effective-product/) | Research, product strategy and design, pricing, and naming |
| [`effective-web`](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/skills/effective-web/) | Browser experiences: UI, React, CSS, accessibility, performance, and testing |
| [`effective-engineering`](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/skills/effective-engineering/) | Architecture, APIs, data systems, Rust, backend TypeScript, and focused tests |
| [`effective-delivery`](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/skills/effective-delivery/) | Repository improvements, PR reviews, dependencies, technical docs, and team delivery |
| [`effective-writing`](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/skills/effective-writing/) | Articles, essays, editing, team communication, and locale typography |
| [`effective-marketing`](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/skills/effective-marketing/) | Positioning, commercial copy, conversion, launches, social content, sales, and CRM |

Optional [instruction packs](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/#instructions)
add standing guidance for request completion and documentation accuracy. Enable
them separately; every skill works without them.

## Installation

With Node.js installed and an agent that supports Agent Skills, add the skill
for your next task. For example, use `effective-web` for frontend work:

```sh
npx skills add sebastian-software/skills.sebastian-software.com --skill effective-web
```

Then ask your agent for an outcome:

> Audit this dashboard, fix the highest-impact accessibility and responsive
> issues, and verify the result.

Replace `effective-web` with any skill from the table. Omit `--skill effective-web`
to choose interactively, or use `--all` to install the collection.

See [installation options](https://skills.sebastian-software.com/#install) or the
[DALO setup guide](docs/dalo.md) for pinned selections, multiple agent targets,
and optional instruction packs. For older skill names, see the
[migration guide](MIGRATION.md).

## Contributing

Improvements should help an agent make a better decision: a clearer trigger,
a missing edge case, or a useful example. Start with the
[authoring guide](docs/authoring-skills.md) and
[contributor setup and checks](docs/contributor-checks.md).

To edit this README, change `README.md.src` and follow the
[README generation workflow](docs/readme-theme.md).

